# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots named with the vulnerable config
# (allow-transfer { any; }) and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the daemon is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, which is what makes
#     the "fixed the config but never restarted the service" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting named cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART (or `rndc reload`) named, not
# merely start it if absent - the daemon is already up with the permissive
# transfer ACL loaded into memory.
